{"id": "EUVD-2026-32798", "enisaUuid": "f18e4921-fc89-340e-af00-4f2b18fe6d42", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nriscv: kvm: fix vector context allocation leak\n\nWhen the second kzalloc (host_context.vector.datap) fails in\nkvm_riscv_vcpu_alloc_vector_context, the first allocation\n(guest_context.vector.datap) is leaked. Free it before returning.", "datePublished": "2026-05-28T09:36:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:41:22", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f3a5dc4055e1001b44ca8ae2bd3eb1d07782049", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/70ecebe7c58ce01f8da3f513eafb51bd147b1e63", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd62c0f61bc722a097417401030c596cea8e21aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1d57ab45ec5c0e22789de793bcf2a31ad6fb7d98", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7c958d7c1eb1cb9b2be7b5ee4129fcd66cec978"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-46171", "GHSA-wxj9-x4vw-8w2j"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "165feef8-31d6-35ca-8591-84bdccb92707", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.7"}, {"id": "18f651ac-bd89-3771-9149-5ef737c9b064", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0f4b82579716b12bb88257bd7ea80f25c791fb2c <b7c958d7c1eb1cb9b2be7b5ee4129fcd66cec978"}, {"id": "245359dc-0d5e-3c5e-a3c2-ba324a7f1b61", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "37d495e6-e5bd-3c02-b80c-10c7e001018c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "5243f60f-21e0-3b20-a13f-61fca5a5b8a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "5f7e7e58-25bd-3b1e-9222-9a4f520b87f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0f4b82579716b12bb88257bd7ea80f25c791fb2c <1d57ab45ec5c0e22789de793bcf2a31ad6fb7d98"}, {"id":